---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Pre-Kindergarten - Marietta Childcare"
  description="Explore Marietta Childcare's Pre-Kindergarten program for ages 4-5 with kindergarten readiness and academic skill development.">
  <section class="relative py-32 overflow-hidden w-screen -ml-[calc((100vw-100%)/2)]">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0">
      <img 
        src="/images/Background_Images/girl_reading_book_quiet_corner_background.jpg" 
        alt="Pre-K learning" 
        class="w-full h-full object-cover"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/40"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-[1280px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-20">
      <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black mb-6 text-white drop-shadow-lg">Pre-Kindergarten Program</h1>
      <p class="text-lg mb-12 max-w-2xl text-white drop-shadow-md">Intensive kindergarten readiness for ages 4-5 with academic skills, social-emotional development, and independence.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20 px-6 lg:px-20">
    <div class="max-w-[1280px] mx-auto">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-3xl mb-12">
        <p>
          Marietta Childcare's Pre-Kindergarten program serves children ages 4 to 5 with intensive kindergarten readiness preparation. The Pre-Kindergarten program at Marietta Childcare focuses on academic skills, social-emotional development, and independence to ensure children are fully prepared for kindergarten success.
        </p>

        <h2>Kindergarten Readiness</h2>
        <p>
          Marietta Childcare's Pre-Kindergarten program emphasizes kindergarten readiness through structured academic instruction and skill development. The Pre-Kindergarten program includes phonics, letter writing, number operations, and early reading skills that prepare children for formal schooling.
        </p>

        <h2>Academic Skills Development</h2>
        <p>
          The Pre-Kindergarten program at Marietta Childcare develops essential academic skills including literacy, numeracy, and critical thinking. Marietta Childcare's educators use research-based instructional strategies to support academic growth and school readiness.
        </p>

        <h2>Social-Emotional Development</h2>
        <p>
          Marietta Childcare recognizes that social-emotional development is crucial for school success. The Pre-Kindergarten program includes activities that develop self-regulation, emotional awareness, cooperation, and conflict resolution skills.
        </p>

        <h2>Independence & Self-Care</h2>
        <p>
          The Pre-Kindergarten program at Marietta Childcare fosters independence and self-care skills essential for kindergarten. Marietta Childcare's pre-K students practice self-directed learning, classroom routines, and responsibility.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-12">
        <div class="bg-primary/5 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-4">Academic Focus</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
            <li>✓ Phonics and reading</li>
            <li>✓ Writing skills</li>
            <li>✓ Math operations</li>
            <li>✓ Science concepts</li>
            <li>✓ Social studies</li>
            <li>✓ Critical thinking</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-secondary/5 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg mb-4">Program Details</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
            <li>✓ Ages 4-5 years</li>
            <li>✓ Full-day programs</li>
            <li>✓ Structured curriculum</li>
            <li>✓ Small class sizes</li>
            <li>✓ Experienced educators</li>
            <li>✓ Parent involvement</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-primary/10 to-secondary/10 p-8 rounded-lg mb-12">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Transition to Kindergarten</h2>
        <p class="mb-6">Marietta Childcare's Pre-Kindergarten program ensures a smooth transition to kindergarten. The Pre-Kindergarten program includes transition activities, kindergarten visits, and parent resources to support successful school entry.</p>
        <a href="/contact" class="inline-block bg-primary text-white px-8 py-3 rounded-full font-bold hover:scale-105 transition-transform">
          Schedule a Tour
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Related Programs & Resources</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <a href="/programs/preschool" class="text-primary font-bold hover:underline">Preschool Program →</a>
          <a href="/resources/school-readiness" class="text-primary font-bold hover:underline">School Readiness Checklist →</a>
          <a href="/faq/transition-to-kindergarten" class="text-primary font-bold hover:underline">Kindergarten Transition →</a>
          <a href="/resources/child-development" class="text-primary font-bold hover:underline">Child Development Guide →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
